 ## Known limitations / todo items
 
-* Only Qualcomm phones supported for now (and only ones that use QMI + QRTR to communicate with the
-  modem, so no 10-year-old phones supported, sorry)
-    * Should work with minor changes on other platforms with an lpac backend, let me know if you can
-      test! => e.g. https://codeberg.org/lucaweiss/lpa-gtk/issues/1
+* QMI, QMI+QRTR and MBIM backends are available. The AT backend currently
+  supports read-only eUICC identification on one typed primary AT endpoint from
+  ModemManager, including empty cards with no MM SIM/EID metadata. lpac must
+  return a valid EID, which must match MM's EID when available and the previously
+  verified EID on later reads. Missing MM metadata leaves physical slot identity
+  unknown. Discovery does not select slots or change cards; multiple candidates
+  require an explicit modem selector, which remains unfinished.
+* AT profile changes remain unfinished: qualify the modem's response behavior
+  for profile-size APDUs and long operations, then implement/qualify channel and
+  late-response recovery after abort. A GUI deadline does not repair a modem's
+  command response limit; this does not mean all AT modems lack support.
+* The AT path requires lpac built with `LPAC_WITH_APDU_AT=ON` and the Unix
+  transport fixes for terminal poll events and complete/EINTR-safe writes.
+  Upstream labels that backend unmaintained; these fixes do not establish
+  profile download support or repair a modem firmware watchdog.
+* AT operations keep one private ModemManager inhibition caller and a pinned
+  endpoint until child reaping. The current AT path supports standard WWAN
+  ports; TTY support needs an acquisition sequence compatible with MM's
+  exclusive ownership. Separate lpac commands do not make card routing
+  atomic. Involuntary D-Bus caller loss can remove inhibition before cleanup;
+  the standard API cannot guarantee reap-before-automatic-uninhibition.
 * No support for scanning QR codes for downloading an eSIM - instead you enter the code starting
   with LPA:1$ into the application => https://codeberg.org/lucaweiss/lpa-gtk/issues/14
